  "answer_text": "Great question! The pronunciation of \"doge\" is actually debated, much like the GIF debate. Here's a breakdown:\n\n---\n\n## How to Pronounce \"Doge\" \ud83d\udc15\n\n### The Most Widely Accepted Pronunciation (The Meme)\nThe most widely accepted pronunciation of Doge (as in the meme/Dogecoin) is **\"dohj\"**, written as **\u02c8d\u0259\u028a\u0292** in the International Phonetic Alphabet.\n\nThis is the pronunciation you'll hear most often in media and online.\n\n---\n\n### Where Did This Come From?\nThis pronunciation was confirmed by Dogecoin's co-creator Jackson Palmer, who said the name was inspired by the animated series *Homestar Runner*. In one of the episodes, a character spells out D-O-G-E and another character reads it as \"dohj\" (d\u0259\u028a\u0292).\n\n---\n\n### All the Common Pronunciations\n\nThere are actually **three** pronunciations in common use:\n\nAccording to Wikipedia, the meme can be pronounced **/do\u028a\u0292/** (\"dohzh\"), **/do\u028ad\u0292/** (\"dohj\"), or **/do\u028a\u0261/** (\"dohg\"), though most media uses /do\u028a\u0292/.\n\n| Pronunciation | Sounds Like | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **dohzh** (/do\u028a\u0292/) | Rhymes with *beige* | Most common in media |\n| **dohj** (/do\u028ad\u0292/) | Rhymes with *dodge* (but with a long O) | Confirmed by the meme's creator |\n| **dohg** (/do\u028a\u0261/) | Like \"dog\" with a long O | Based on spelling logic |\n\n---\n\n### Common Mispronunciations to Avoid\nSome of the common mispronunciations include \"doggycoin\", \"dogcoin\", and \"dodgecoin\".\n\n---\n\n### Bottom Line\nMuch like the GIF debate, both the hard G (like \"dog\") and the soft G (like \"dohj\") are in common use and can both be justified with reasonable explanations. However, if you want to go with the creator's intended pronunciation, say **\"dohj\"** \u2014 rhyming roughly with \"dodge\" but with a long O sound.",
